            <ArticleTitle>Oxidative Dehomologation of Aldehydes with Oxygen as a Terminal Oxidant.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6760-6762</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03512</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A mild, efficient protocol for oxidative cleavage of C-C bonds in aldehydes has been developed that employs alkali metal hydrides as reagents and oxygen from air as a terminal oxidant. The method is applicable to a broad substrate range.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
